## Safety Rule (human-in-the-loop)

The agent may **prepare** these actions but must **not execute them autonomously** —
they require explicit human/operator approval:

```text
external communication            scope changes
proposal acceptance               production deployment
payment confirmation              destructive database operations (DROP, migrate reset)
secret exposure                   provider token usage
resource deletion                 protected-branch push (main / develop)
final delivery approval           commercial commitments
```

When such an action is needed: generate the draft / migration / plan, then create a
blocker in `docs/develop/AGENT_PROGRESS.md` requesting approval. Do not proceed.

Never deploy without approval. Never modify production secrets. Never rewrite git history.
Never push to `main` or `develop`.

