## Skills and Subagents

Use selectively (do not invoke every skill automatically):

- `execute-sprint` skill / `sprint-runner` agent: the main autonomous loop.
- `verify-feature` skill / `test-engineer` agent: before marking a batch DONE.
- `code-reviewer` agent: before committing meaningful changes.
- `architect-reviewer` agent: when changes touch module boundaries, state machines or the data model.
- `debug-failure` skill: when typecheck/lint/test/build fails.
- `update-progress` skill: after completing, pausing or blocking work.

General dev skills (also injected into the night runner via `--append-system-prompt`, see
`scripts/claude-night-runner.ps1`):

- `ponytail:ponytail`: **on every implementation step** — laziest solution that actually works
  (reuse existing code, stdlib/native before new deps, shortest correct diff, no speculative
  abstractions; delete over add). Most important; keeps the MVP inside scope.
- `superpowers:test-driven-development`: when implementing domain logic (state machines,
  orchestration, proposal/budget rules) — failing test first.
- `superpowers:systematic-debugging`: on any failure, before editing — root cause over symptom
  (pairs with `debug-failure`).
- `superpowers:verification-before-completion`: before marking a batch DONE or claiming pass — run
  the verification sequence, confirm real output (pairs with `verify-feature`).

